{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-tail-start","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0341","math_ordinal":29,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The partial-sum difference S_m-S_{n_k} is generated by increments with i strictly greater than n_k; including X_{n_k} would shift the Etemadi sequence by one term.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:63","source_normalized_sha256":"32c421b9b9e765a58a923fb691391bda77925f6f9cee56507b50ee23820cb35d","source_text":"\\langle X_i\\rangle_{i\\ge n_k}","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:63","target_normalized_sha256":"baa4a8a1e0e184a3b92be389d645ed4968ec35758e08029bf004e5ab6271878d","target_text":"\\langle X_i\\rangle_{i>n_k}","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0342","math_ordinal":80,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof estimates the finite sum of deviations x-x_i. Without parentheses the summation binds only x and leaves one free x_i outside it.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:147","source_normalized_sha256":"7f045a871e24fd61be0d5cc1d770c7475eefff7a8ada2c35a964726eecfa5dd5","source_text":"|\\sum_{i=0}^{m-1}x-x_i|","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:150","target_normalized_sha256":"2621b69bb60720af4857485519fe98459ae5af2e482bf9ef50e162cfac1a56cd","target_text":"|\\sum_{i=0}^{m-1}(x-x_i)|","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0343","math_ordinal":82,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Both displayed sums are sums of deviations; the printed ungrouped forms leave the indexed x_i outside the summation operator and do not yield the stated Cesaro estimate.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:150-154","source_normalized_sha256":"c86e5c36a367399c0b9a5c06105788492d4cae76dc89667d9ac01eac8fd7f923","source_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^nx-x_i","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:153-158","target_normalized_sha256":"08fdc1b313555028d6b28adfaea6aa96457633e508ec76d1777af0aea29d2e24","target_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n(x-x_i)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-invalid-initial-terms","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0344","math_ordinal":131,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"As written the example is undefined at n=0 and equals zero at n=1, contradicting the theorem's strictly positive sequence hypothesis. Restricting the formula to n>=2 and choosing positive initial terms preserves the intended eventual example.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:257","source_normalized_sha256":"2e90ae8fb85e178af00aa8b39a682ea9cebb4cbd1a5f8cd7b6ada8fcc7d2e05e","source_text":"b_n=\\sqrt{n}\\ln n","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:261-263","target_normalized_sha256":"4f75f5d33232a7995c4cffc4e4215d4a454dc0257b0cb465357f52ac6e5067b4","target_text":"b_n=\\sqrt{n}\\ln n\\quad(n\\ge 2)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-zero-index-boundary","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0345","math_ordinal":171,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The displayed variance estimate uses n^{1-delta}; the proof must state it for n>=1, while Y_0=0 is handled separately.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:344","source_normalized_sha256":"02bb197ae0de627eb1861382dcf81826f92f1895770d739be7f05b2435488186","source_text":"n\\in\\Bbb N","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:351","target_normalized_sha256":"37da60206b14e06bf71351a297c4bf5db7653b3a6defb20cd4a5b8d8af1cd1ae","target_text":"n\\ge 1","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-zero-index-boundary","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0346","math_ordinal":174,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The n=0 comparison is undefined or ambiguous when delta=1, whereas Y_0=0. Separating that term and starting the comparison at one makes the convergence estimate valid for the stated range.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:351-353","source_normalized_sha256":"7050c618030eea63f0415e75dd83991d792be1389af21957ff4253787370a9be","source_text":"\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}\\Bover{n^{1-\\delta}}{(n+1)^2}K","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:356-359","target_normalized_sha256":"eae7328fa14fb23a011771f98fc48e8074b50b7494d0a577f952299df9d2cc90","target_text":"\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\Bover{n^{1-\\delta}}{(n+1)^2}K","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-limit-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0347","math_ordinal":186,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The convergence statement concerns the difference of the two expectations for each n. Without parentheses only the first term is under the limit and X_n remains free.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:391","source_normalized_sha256":"42e4bd1faced214aac2316c540e54848e202ec2b06c237925f865abe8442e1f1","source_text":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\Expn(Y_n)-\\Expn(X_n)=0","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:400","target_normalized_sha256":"8dd80c90e1aaeabb3877f98c00e0ecbb661596a2f766285f5c5971881a67e131","target_text":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(\\Expn(Y_n)-\\Expn(X_n))=0","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0348","math_ordinal":187,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The Cesaro step averages the expectation differences. The printed form leaves one X_i term outside the sum.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:393-394","source_normalized_sha256":"b67d5707b1ff9ffe2838eb15ce4cd21350f524edb19130be7b6431866bbaef3e","source_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n\\Expn(Y_i)-\\Expn(X_i)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:402-403","target_normalized_sha256":"62e765cb682b7a556c730b5ad3eeb93bd7dc184324dca224cbda700a3d5be546","target_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n(\\Expn(Y_i)-\\Expn(X_i))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0349","math_ordinal":188,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The strong-law average centers every X_i; without parentheses only the X_i values are summed and one unbound expectation is subtracted.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:398-400","source_normalized_sha256":"5e55ea960b5f62cdb4ea3046637411665bd9a969eb3733c90d82f2bc6e5f4377","source_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^nX_i(\\omega)-\\Expn(X_i)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:407-408","target_normalized_sha256":"5b46e4eb04458d02bd33d88da489df0d085de314335e53bd97eabbde0701770d","target_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n(X_i(\\omega)-\\Expn(X_i))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0350","math_ordinal":191,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The final almost-everywhere statement repeats the centered sum and requires the same per-summand grouping.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:404-406","source_normalized_sha256":"a36780599ff221f95efc2bc009090fe5640d0235df27fbe6c937970c8d9b2756","source_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^nX_i-\\Expn(X_i)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:413-414","target_normalized_sha256":"ddd38c8e61d1feac513ce356bfe717f692a9873c4cb2f8c5175ba822bee5d3fd","target_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n(X_i-\\Expn(X_i))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0351","math_ordinal":234,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The truncation argument averages each difference X_i-Y_i; the printed expression subtracts only one free Y_i after summing the X_i.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:516","source_normalized_sha256":"6666280361eb47083b84725e78d5a53bcbc4ad79a213e4e89811b5326630d3f8","source_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^nX_i(\\omega)-Y_i(\\omega)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:525-526","target_normalized_sha256":"a05867f2d293b0c0e67015cd110b91407cc74034ed4a560415ef3c61fe7eb648","target_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n(X_i(\\omega)-Y_i(\\omega))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-limit-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0352","math_ordinal":238,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The repeated convergence statement concerns the difference for each n; the ungrouped source leaves X_n outside the limit.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:529","source_normalized_sha256":"42e4bd1faced214aac2316c540e54848e202ec2b06c237925f865abe8442e1f1","source_text":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\Expn(Y_n)-\\Expn(X_n)=0","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:539","target_normalized_sha256":"8dd80c90e1aaeabb3877f98c00e0ecbb661596a2f766285f5c5971881a67e131","target_text":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(\\Expn(Y_n)-\\Expn(X_n))=0","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0353","math_ordinal":239,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The second strong-law proof repeats the Cesaro average of expectation differences and needs the same grouping.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:531","source_normalized_sha256":"b67d5707b1ff9ffe2838eb15ce4cd21350f524edb19130be7b6431866bbaef3e","source_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n\\Expn(Y_i)-\\Expn(X_i)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:541-542","target_normalized_sha256":"62e765cb682b7a556c730b5ad3eeb93bd7dc184324dca224cbda700a3d5be546","target_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n(\\Expn(Y_i)-\\Expn(X_i))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0354","math_ordinal":240,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The second proof's pointwise centered sum requires the expectation inside each summand.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:536","source_normalized_sha256":"5e55ea960b5f62cdb4ea3046637411665bd9a969eb3733c90d82f2bc6e5f4377","source_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^nX_i(\\omega)-\\Expn(X_i)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:546-547","target_normalized_sha256":"5b46e4eb04458d02bd33d88da489df0d085de314335e53bd97eabbde0701770d","target_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n(X_i(\\omega)-\\Expn(X_i))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0355","math_ordinal":243,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The concluding almost-everywhere centered average repeats the same source grouping defect.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:542","source_normalized_sha256":"a36780599ff221f95efc2bc009090fe5640d0235df27fbe6c937970c8d9b2756","source_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^nX_i-\\Expn(X_i)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:552-553","target_normalized_sha256":"ddd38c8e61d1feac513ce356bfe717f692a9873c4cb2f8c5175ba822bee5d3fd","target_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n(X_i-\\Expn(X_i))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0356","math_ordinal":260,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The product-space application invokes the centered strong law and must subtract each expectation inside the summation.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:584","source_normalized_sha256":"5fc8432b65e7b01d9d923015396f0e2c02b065e601191d40b37c5cf9a909a931","source_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^nX_i(\\pmb{\\omega})-\\Expn(X_i)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:594","target_normalized_sha256":"00716dd9d9317bc0cd0f3266bc378acd2a6dd66f25582554cca2a9f3787bbb5a","target_text":"\\sum_{i=0}^n(X_i(\\pmb{\\omega})-\\Expn(X_i))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-summand-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0357","math_ordinal":292,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Beta_n is E(X_n), the sum of the first n+1 event probabilities. The printed E_n factor is constant across the sum and contradicts the next variance computation.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:664","source_normalized_sha256":"30c3b3e874de3010c54eb57e7a243a49015ef93d5dc8c303b1fd1f43a81087ed","source_text":"\\beta_n=\\sum_{i=0}^n\\mu E_n","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:675","target_normalized_sha256":"80751cb53ccc0da06a3d9085a22de09f47455e63216eb47eac039313b73ef42b","target_text":"\\beta_n=\\sum_{i=0}^n\\mu E_i","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-upper-bound-and-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0358","math_ordinal":311,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The example concerns the nth centered average. An infinite upper bound makes the displayed numerator independent of n and the ungrouped expectation leaves i free.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:717-718","source_normalized_sha256":"17b99e44ed5608d2d2ba295ff0b1d0c50f7114bd32feb076fa60e149c742d021","source_text":"\\limsup_{n\\to\\infty}\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^{\\infty}X_i-\\Expn(X_i)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:728-729","target_normalized_sha256":"118c5d66d0f9d346d6b1111c2cc56faafb4f6bed35b7b4ce911fad8210300d69","target_text":"\\limsup_{n\\to\\infty}\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^{n}(X_i-\\Expn(X_i))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-upper-bound-and-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0359","math_ordinal":312,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The companion liminf statement has the same two defects and must use the nth centered partial sum.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:720-721","source_normalized_sha256":"757702a469e6074b370ec15a73116c41ed6c50099f6fa5a85293aa776e2701a0","source_text":"\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^{\\infty}X_i-\\Expn(X_i)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:731-732","target_normalized_sha256":"69410941c2db4e79ca8fe56a8bc89a4a62441f14be6a4b186a8daffcf382f9ad","target_text":"\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^{n}(X_i-\\Expn(X_i))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-unmatched-norm-delimiter","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0360","math_ordinal":406,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The printed right parenthesis has no matching left parenthesis and interrupts the sum of the two Lp norms; removing it restores the norm expression used throughout the proof.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:869","source_normalized_sha256":"fe34a3aafa7c40f2cc3b432e1867c9417fab512bf7bfd626497312215af2d7ad","source_text":"\\|X\\times\\chi F)\\|_p","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:886","target_normalized_sha256":"f0bfa5043989275a2f8ca599eb49891910284f89988bff31ffcc52fe4d84201f","target_text":"\\|X\\times\\chi F\\|_p","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-average-decomposition","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0361","math_ordinal":445,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Since Y_n is the average of X_0 through X_n and X_i=tilde X_i+X''_i+alpha_i, its scalar component is the average of all alpha_i, not the final alpha_n. The following bound must use the same average.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:974-976","source_normalized_sha256":"0f67149d99188f6351ab89f1e9e5f34c7fa3d86f5d475af505f0b1d23f6a0209","source_text":"\\tilde Y_n+Y''_n+\\alpha_n","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:994-999","target_normalized_sha256":"cc368684754cfce3fe153360a4c534341998d90d7ad8d552988ab06d90797189","target_text":"\\tilde Y_n+Y''_n+\\Bover1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^n\\alpha_i","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-primes","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0362","math_ordinal":596,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The note explicitly discusses the uniformly bounded variables X'_n; the displayed average accidentally drops the primes and refers to the original sequence instead.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt273.tex:1202","source_normalized_sha256":"e534a894129337b4c0e0a747437c265917708f398f4bd7e8f8d5fce9f33d8a4e","source_text":"(X_0+\\ldots+X_n)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt273.tex:1235","target_normalized_sha256":"bf1199be49da5927aa318b3a2181f2e0699b3a25cef226c0507391701f81b2db","target_text":"(X'_0+\\ldots+X'_n)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S273"}
